# AI providers, tried in the order below until one answers.
#
# Every provider here speaks the OpenAI /chat/completions shape. A provider with
# no key set is SKIPPED, not attempted, so leaving a line commented out is the
# supported way to turn one off. At least one must be set or the commentary and
# verse-detective routes return 503 with a readable sentence.
#
# Check what is live at any time:  GET /api/ai-health

# 1. NVIDIA NIM. Free, OpenAI-compatible, currently the primary.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to mistralai/mistral-medium-3.5-128b.
# NVIDIA_MODEL=
# Optional extra models on this provider, comma separated, tried after the primary.
# NVIDIA_FALLBACK_MODELS=

# 2. Groq. Free tier, very fast. The most useful second link because it is a
#    different company on different infrastructure, which is the only kind of
#    redundancy that survives an outage at the first one.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# 3. Gemini, through Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# 4. OpenAI. Paid, so it is last and normally unset.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# 5. Ollama, for local development only. Deliberately has NO default: a
#    deployed function cannot reach localhost, and an unset value must mean
#    "not available here" rather than "try 127.0.0.1 and wait for the timeout".
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1

# Override the order. Default: nvidia,groq,gemini,openai,ollama
# AI_PROVIDER_ORDER=nvidia,groq
